# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js 16.3.0 project using the App Router.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Package**: `@vercel/analytics` (version 1.4.1)
- **Package Manager**: npm
- **Installation Method**: `npm install @vercel/analytics`

### 2. Configuration Files Modified

#### frontend/package.json
- Added `@vercel/analytics` to dependencies

#### frontend/package-lock.json
- Updated with new package and its 655 dependencies
- No vulnerabilities detected

#### frontend/src/app/layout.tsx
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` element, after the `<Providers>` component

## Implementation Details

### Framework Detection
This project uses:
- **Framework**: Next.js 16.3.0
- **Router**: App Router (confirmed by presence of `src/app/layout.tsx`)
- **Language**: TypeScript

### Documentation Source
Fetched the latest installation instructions from the official Vercel documentation:
- URL: https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Instructions followed: Next.js (App Router) specific guidelines

### Code Changes
The Analytics component was added to the root layout file following the official Next.js App Router pattern:
- Import from `@vercel/analytics/next`
- Component placed inside the `<body>` element
- Preserves all existing functionality and code structure

